配链路，加入对空心精灵的轮廓化放置说明与辅助函数\n  ✓ 实现 generator：生成带洞且轮廓化后保留双边界的精灵，并用 output-first 校验\n  ✓ 运行 50 次稳定性测试与融合行为统计，必要时迭代修正\ndiff --git a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/16/code.py b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/16/code.py\nindex 5a7374dfc2090b33a2ae17988f897a423bc1915f..0ce70327938a315d190d3e3756f457eb7ca0f8b6\n--- a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/16/code.py\n+++ b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/16/code.py\n@@ -10,106 +10,55 @@\n from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n \n \n-# Design analysis\n-# ---------------\n-# a) Concrete behavior:\n-#    - Original edb79dae copies a same-colored sprite from outside the frame into\n-#      each solid placeholder block, then recolors it via the external legend.\n-#    - This combo changes the source object itself and the placement rule:\n-#      external sprites are already hollow, meaning their bbox contains at least\n-#      one enclosed bg component, and the copied result keeps only the sprite's\n-#      4-neighbor contour pixels.\n-#    - Small trace with a 5x5 source sprite:\n-#        source sprite:\n-#          11111\n-#          11111\n-#          11011\n-#          11111\n-#          11111\n-#        D3-only placement would paste that thick hollow ring as-is.\n-#        Combo placement first extracts the contour, so interior cells such as\n-#        (1,1), (1,3), (3,1), (3,3) survive only if they touch outer bg or the\n-#        inner hole; fully surrounded cells are removed. The output becomes a\n-#        thinner nested outline around both the outside boundary and the hole.\n-#    - The observable difference from the original task is therefore twofold:\n-#      the input templates visibly contain holes, and the output thins those\n-#      hollow shapes further instead of stamping the full mask.\n-#\n-# b) Complexity calibration:\n-#    - The generator restricts sprite size to 4-5 instead of allowing 3. Size 3\n-#      hollow masks usually collapse into one-pixel-thick rings where D5 becomes\n-#      invisible, so excluding them keeps the fused effect observable.\n-#    - Placeholder colors are capped at 2-4 and each chosen color is used at\n-#      least twice inside the frame. That keeps the scene readable and repeats\n-#      the same transformed hollow template multiple times.\n-#    - Every generated sprite must satisfy three checks simultaneously:\n-#      it has at least one enclosed hole, outlining removes at least one pixel,\n-#      and the outlined result is still non-empty. This prevents silent\n-#      regression to plain D3 or plain D5 behavior.\n-#\n-# c) Old assumptions that must change:\n-#    - The original solver effectively assumed an outside sprite mask could be\n-#      written back directly. That is no longer valid; the solver must rebuild\n-#      a mask, outline it, and only then stamp it.\n-#    - Hollow sprites introduce bg inside the bbox, but this does not break\n-#      placeholder detection because placeholders inside the frame remain solid\n-#      NxN blocks.\n-#    - Legend parsing still relies on compact two-color overlapping glyphs with\n-#      no bg in their union bbox. Because sprites and legends are placed with a\n-#      full-bbox reserve mask, hollow sprite holes cannot leak into legend bboxes.\n-#    - The \"one size-matched sprite per placeholder color\" assumption still\n-#      holds because the generator keeps exactly one external template bbox for\n-#      each source color and keeps legends at fixed 3x4 size.\n-#\n-# d) Placement legality:\n-#    - Inside the frame, placeholders still live on an NxN grid with one-cell bg\n-#      gaps, so even outlined hollow sprites never overlap after stamping.\n-#    - Outside the frame, both legends and sprites reserve their full bboxes plus\n-#      padding, so no two patches overlap and no legend can sit inside a sprite\n-#      hole.\n-#    - The generator is output-first: it constructs the expected outlined-hollow\n-#      output frame, backfills the input placeholders and external cues, then\n-#      runs `main()` as an oracle.\n-#\n-# e) Visual observability:\n-#    - A human can see the hollow-source rule directly because every outside\n-#      sprite has an enclosed bg hole. A human can see the outline-placement\n-#      rule because the frame output is thinner than the external template while\n-#      preserving the inner-hole boundary.\n-#    - No ordering depends on numeric color ids. Colors only serve as visible\n-#      equality keys: placeholder color selects the source sprite, and legend\n-#      pairing selects the final recolor.\n-#\n-# f) Visual cleanliness:\n-#    - Sprites stay small and thick enough to show nested contours cleanly.\n-#      Reducing the number of placeholder colors avoids a noisy legend field.\n-#    - Targets are recolored uniformly per source color, and the frame border plus\n-#      bg gaps keep the transformed regions visually separated.\n-#\n-# g) Change inferability:\n-#    - The recoloring rule remains structurally explained by the same outside\n-#      legends as the original task, so the only new inference burden is local:\n-#      \"copy the hollow sprite, but keep only its contour pixels.\"\n-#    - Because each grid repeats source colors multiple times, the solver gets\n-#      repeated evidence that the same hollow template is reused consistently.\n-#\n-# Post-change solver assumptions reviewed against the generator:\n-#    - Every placeholder color has exactly one non-legend sprite bbox of the same\n-#      size: guaranteed.\n-#    - Every external sprite has >=1 enclosed hole: guaranteed by `_hole_count`.\n-#    - Every external sprite loses pixels under outlining: guaranteed by\n-#      `_outline_mask(mask).sum() < mask.sum()`.\n-#    - Outlined masks stay non-empty and fit exactly inside placeholder bboxes:\n-#      guaranteed.\n-#    - Legends use target colors outside the placeholder-color set, so legend\n-#      source/target inference remains unambiguous.\n+# Design analysis for the D3/1 + D5/3 combo\n+# ------------------------------------------\n+# variant:\n+#   concrete_trace:\n+#     原题里，框外同色精灵通常是实心/普通单色模板，框内输出直接复制整块形状再按图例重着色。\n+#     融合后，框外模板先升级为“空心精灵”：\n+#       例如 5x5 `11111/11111/11011/11111/11111`，中心 0 被同色像素包围，是一个内部洞。\n+#     若只做 D3/1，框内会得到同样的带洞形状；若只做 D5/3，实心精灵会被削成单层外轮廓。\n+#     这里两者叠加时，轮廓定义按像素连通区域边界处理：任何拥有上/下/左/右四个同色邻居\n+#     的像素都被挖空。于是上例会变成\n+#       `11111/10101/11011/10101/11111`\n+#     输出同时保留外边界和围绕内部洞的内边界，这个“双轮廓”正是融合后的核心可观察行为。\n+#   complexity_guardrails:\n+#     - 若空心精灵只有 1 像素厚的环，轮廓化后可能与原空心精灵完全相同，D5 会退化。\n+#     - 若精灵没有内部洞，则会退化成单独的 D5/3。\n+#     因此生成器强制每个模板同时满足：\n+#       1. bbox 内存在至少一个封闭背景洞；\n+#       2. 轮廓化会删除至少若干个像素；\n+#       3. 轮廓结果中存在紧邻洞的像素，确保内边界真实出现。\n+#   solver_assumption_audit:\n+#     - `_find_frame` 只依赖唯一矩形框，融合不改这点。\n+#     - 框内占位块仍是实心单色 NxN 方块，所以 placeholder 收集逻辑可复用。\n+#     - 图例仍是紧凑双色无背景重叠块；空心精灵因自身 bbox 中含背景洞，不会被误判成图例。\n+#     - 原 solver 默认“把外部模板的前景坐标原样写回”。融合后必须先重建模板掩码，\n+#       再取 4 邻域轮廓；此轮廓规则天然会同时保留外边界和内洞边界。\n+#     - 外部精灵仍按 bbox 与占位块同尺寸匹配，所以生成器必须保证模板四周都有前景，\n+#       不能因挖洞导致 bbox 缩小。\n+#   generator_legality:\n+#     - 继续使用 output-first：先用“空心模板的轮廓化结果”生成目标输出，再回填输入占位块。\n+#     - 框内仍是规则网格且块间至少 1 格背景，双轮廓模板互不接触。\n+#     - 框外继续通过 reserve 网格和 padding 放置精灵与图例，保证不重叠、不越界。\n+#   visual_observability:\n+#     - 颜色只用于同色匹配和图例重着色，不依赖颜色数值大小。\n+#     - 精灵尺寸固定在足够显示洞与双轮廓的范围，且同色通常在框内重复出现，\n+#       解题者可在 2-4 个样例里稳定看到“带洞模板 -> 双边界轮廓”的规律。\n+#   cleanliness:\n+#     框外负责提供原始带洞模板和颜色图例；框内只展示变换结果。层次没有叠在同一区域，\n+#     因此双轮廓结构肉眼可分辨，不会和图例/占位块混淆。\n+#   new_solver_assumptions:\n+#     - 每个外部模板必须至少有一个封闭洞，且轮廓化后仍保留非空像素。\n+#     - 轮廓定义采用 4 邻域“非内点保留”，生成器与 solver 复用同一实现，避免语义漂移。\n \n \n def _find_frame(g: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> tuple[int, tuple[int, int, int, int]]:\n     \"\"\"\n     Find a rectangular border component:\n       - all bbox-border cells are this color,\n-      - bbox-interior is not entirely this color.\n+      - bbox-interior is not entirely this color,\n+      - bbox-interior contains at least one non-bg, non-frame pixel.\n     Return (frame_color, (r0,c0,r1,c1)).\n     \"\"\"\n     candidates = []\n@@ -129,14 +78,23 @@\n                 continue\n             if np.all(sub[~border] == col):\n                 continue\n+            inner_vals = set(map(int, np.unique(sub[1:-1, 1:-1])))\n+            if not any(v not in (bg, col) for v in inner_vals):\n+                continue\n             candidates.append((col, (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n     assert len(candidates) == 1, f\"expected exactly one rectangular frame component, found {len(candidates)}\"\n     frame_col, bbox = candidates[0]\n     return int(frame_col), bbox\n \n \n+def _bbox_overlap(a: tuple[int, int, int, int], b: tuple[int, int, int, int]) -> bool:\n+    ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = a\n+    br0, bc0, br1, bc1 = b\n+    return not (ar1 < br0 or br1 < ar0 or ac1 < bc0 or bc1 < ac0)\n+\n+\n def _outline_mask(mask: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n-    \"\"\"Keep foreground pixels that touch bg or the bbox exterior in 4-neighborhood.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Keep every boundary pixel of a binary shape under 4-neighbor interior removal.\"\"\"\n     mask = np.asarray(mask, dtype=bool)\n     interior = np.zeros_like(mask, dtype=bool)\n     if mask.shape[0] >= 3 and mask.shape[1] >= 3:\n@@ -150,35 +108,61 @@\n     return mask & ~interior\n \n \n-def _hole_count(mask: np.ndarray) -> int:\n-    \"\"\"Count bg components fully enclosed by the foreground inside the bbox.\"\"\"\n-    inv = ~np.asarray(mask, dtype=bool)\n-    count = 0\n-    for pts in components_mask(inv, connectivity=4):\n-        rr = pts[:, 0]\n-        cc = pts[:, 1]\n-        if np.any(rr == 0) or np.any(rr == inv.shape[0] - 1) or np.any(cc == 0) or np.any(cc == inv.shape[1] - 1):\n-            continue\n-        count += 1\n-    return count\n+def _hole_mask(mask: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n+    \"\"\"Return enclosed background cells inside a sprite mask.\"\"\"\n+    mask = np.asarray(mask, dtype=bool)\n+    holes = np.zeros_like(mask, dtype=bool)\n+    for pts in components_mask(~mask, connectivity=4):\n+        rows = pts[:, 0]\n+        cols = pts[:, 1]\n+        if np.all((rows > 0) & (rows < mask.shape[0] - 1) & (cols > 0) & (cols < mask.shape[1] - 1)):\n+            holes[rows, cols] = True\n+    return holes\n+\n+\n+def _sprite_metrics(mask: np.ndarray) -> dict[str, int]:\n+    \"\"\"Quantify whether the combo behavior is actually visible on a sprite.\"\"\"\n+    mask = np.asarray(mask, dtype=bool)\n+    outline = _outline_mask(mask)\n+    holes = _hole_mask(mask)\n+    inner_boundary = 0\n+    for r, c in np.argwhere(outline):\n+        if (\n+            (r > 0 and holes[r - 1, c])\n+            or (r + 1 < holes.shape[0] and holes[r + 1, c])\n+            or (c > 0 and holes[r, c - 1])\n+            or (c + 1 < holes.shape[1] and holes[r, c + 1])\n+        ):\n+            inner_boundary += 1\n+    return {\n+        \"holes\": int(holes.any()),\n+        \"removed\": int(mask.sum() - outline.sum()),\n+        \"inner_boundary\": int(inner_boundary),\n+    }\n+\n \n+def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n+    \"\"\"\n+    Recolor and place outlined hollow sprites into the framed workspace.\n \n-def _foreground_component_count(mask: np.ndarray) -> int:\n-    return len(components_mask(np.asarray(mask, dtype=bool), connectivity=4))\n+    Input structure:\n+    - The canvas has one rectangular gray frame whose interior contains solid-color placeholder blocks.\n+    - Outside the frame, each placeholder color has a same-color sprite template; these templates are hollow shapes with enclosed background holes.\n+    - The outside area also contains compact two-color legend glyphs that map placeholder colors to their final output colors.\n \n+    Rule:\n+    - Detect the frame, collect placeholder blocks inside it, and recover the matching same-color hollow sprite for each placeholder color.\n+    - Use the legend glyphs to determine the recoloring target for each placeholder color.\n+    - Before stamping a sprite into the frame, convert the sprite to its 4-neighbor contour: keep every foreground pixel on the boundary of the connected region and erase only strict interior pixels.\n+    - Paste that contour at every placeholder position and recolor it with the legend-selected output color, while preserving the frame border and background.\n \n-def _collect_scene(\n-    grid: np.ndarray,\n-) -> tuple[\n-    int,\n-    np.ndarray,\n-    list[tuple[int, tuple[int, int, int, int]]],\n-    dict[int, int],\n-    dict[int, np.ndarray],\n-]:\n-    \"\"\"Parse the input into frame crop, placeholders, legend map, and raw sprite masks.\"\"\"\n+    Key insight:\n+    - Placeholder color still selects the template and the legend still selects the final color.\n+    - The fused step is that the source template already has a hole, and contour extraction is applied to the whole foreground region, so the output keeps both the outer boundary and the boundary around the hole.\n+    \"\"\"\n     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n     bg = get_bg(g)\n+\n     frame_col, (fr0, fc0, fr1, fc1) = _find_frame(g, bg)\n \n     crop = g[fr0 : fr1 + 1, fc0 : fc1 + 1]\n@@ -225,11 +209,6 @@\n             )\n             cid += 1\n \n-    def _bbox_overlap(a: tuple[int, int, int, int], b: tuple[int, int, int, int]) -> bool:\n-        ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = a\n-        br0, bc0, br1, bc1 = b\n-        return not (ar1 < br0 or br1 < ar0 or ac1 < bc0 or bc1 < ac0)\n-\n     color_map: dict[int, int] = {}\n     legend_ids: set[int] = set()\n \n@@ -276,7 +255,7 @@\n         f\"legend mappings {sorted(color_map)} do not match placeholders {sorted(placeholder_colors)}\"\n     )\n \n-    sprite_masks: dict[int, np.ndarray] = {}\n+    sprite_coords: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int]] = {}\n     for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n         all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n         assert all_candidates, f\"no non-legend sprite found for color {src_col}\"\